<article class="env-lemma" id="0F6U">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F6U">Lemma <span data-tag="0F6U">63.6.5</span>.</a> Consider a cartesian square </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X' \ar[r]_{g'} \ar[d]_{f'} &  X \ar[d]^ f \\  Y' \ar[r]^ g &  Y }  \]
</div>
  <p> of schemes with $f$ locally quasi-finite. For any abelian sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $Y'_{\acute{e}tale}$ we have $(g')_*(f')^!\mathcal{F} = f^!g_*\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By uniqueness of adjoint functors, this follows from the corresponding (dual) statement for the functors $f_!$. See Lemma <a href="/tag/0F5J" data-tag="0F5J">63.4.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>